From 639bf8598de5ef0e8fee6ac190429c1493c6b7b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Decodere <98278826+Decodere@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:19:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] dxil: prefer live lanes in PS v_readfirstlane and
 lane-mask SCC tests

Bring the direct DXIL pixel-shader lowering into parity with the HLSL
recompiler's live-lane handling for helper lanes under s_wqm:

- lanes.rs: add Lw::is_pixel (reused in ballot and rla) and
  Lw::live_lanes (WaveActiveBallot(true), selecting the active half in
  wave32-in-64 mode). Update Lw::first_lane so pixel shaders intersect
  EXEC with live lanes before firstbitlow when any live lane is set,
  falling back to the raw mask otherwise (parity with first_lane_live).
- lower.rs: add Lw::ps_mask_live_scc and mask only the SCC zero-check
  (leaving the destination register unmasked) for pixel-shader ENC_SOP2
  s_and_b32 / s_andn2_b32 / s_and_b64 / s_andn2_b64 instructions that
  reference VCC (106) or EXEC (126) (parity with mask_live, extended to
  64-bit masks).
- lanes.rs (ps_ballot_tests): add DXC-validated disassembly tests with
  non-mask and compute negative controls plus a two-triangle edge GPU
  test covering v_readfirstlane, helper-only s_andn2 SCC, unmasked
  destination preservation, and the 6-pass march loop shape.

Part of #675
Part of #1401
Part of #1833

